  "question": "1) Background / Context\n\nDjango is a high-level Python web framework designed to facilitate rapid development and clean, pragmatic design. It offers a comprehensive platform for developers to build web applications without the need to reinvent common components. Django streamlines web development, provides robust security features, and offers scalability for high-traffic applications.\n\n2) Objectives\n\nThe primary goal is to provide a framework that supports fast development of web applications, ensuring a secure and scalable environment. Django aims to handle common web development tasks efficiently, allowing developers to focus on creating the core functionality of their applications.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Developers: Utilize Django to expedite the development process of web applications.\n- Administrators: Manage user accounts, permissions, and additional backend tasks.\n- End-users: Interact with web applications built on the Django framework.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- Rapid Development: Facilitate quick project turnaround from concept to deployment.\n- Comprehensive Features: Include user authentication, content management, site maps, RSS feeds, and more.\n- Security: Protect against SQL injections, cross-site scripting, and other common vulnerabilities.\n- User Management: Support secure user authentication and permission management through a robust admin interface.\n- Data Logging: Track changes and activities within the system using the Django admin log.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Scalability: Support scaling to meet high traffic demands efficiently.\n- Flexibility: Allow versatile application design, suitable for various types of projects from CMS to social networks.\n- Open Source: Provide a free and community-supported framework, encouraging contributions and enhancements.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0022\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(150) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(254) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(128) NOT NULL,\n  `is_active` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '1',\n  `is_staff` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `is_superuser` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `date_joined` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `username` (`username`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `groups` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(150) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `name` (`name`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `permissions` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `codename` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `content_type` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `permission_unique` (`content_type`,`codename`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_groups` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `group_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `user_group_unique` (`user_id`,`group_id`),\n  KEY `user_groups_ibfk_2` (`group_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_groups_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_groups_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`group_id`) REFERENCES `groups` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `group_permissions` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `group_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `permission_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `group_permission_unique` (`group_id`,`permission_id`),\n  KEY `group_permissions_ibfk_2` (`permission_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `group_permissions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`group_id`) REFERENCES `groups` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `group_permissions_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`permission_id`) REFERENCES `permissions` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_permissions` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `permission_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `user_permission_unique` (`user_id`,`permission_id`),\n  KEY `user_permissions_ibfk_2` (`permission_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_permissions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_permissions_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`permission_id`) REFERENCES `permissions` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sites` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `domain` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `domain` (`domain`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `content_types` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `app_label` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `model` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `content_type_unique` (`app_label`,`model`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `admin_log` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `action_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `content_type_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `object_id` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `object_repr` varchar(200) NOT NULL,\n  `action_flag` smallint(5) NOT NULL,\n  `change_message` longtext NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `admin_log_ibfk_1` (`user_id`),\n  KEY `admin_log_ibfk_2` (`content_type_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `admin_log_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `admin_log_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`content_type_id`) REFERENCES `content_types` (`id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
